 had an  additional set of arms and legs doxies  had shiny beetle-like wings and a double  row of sharp teeth  6. dear recall the direcol known to  muggles as the dodo was a plump fluffy  feathered and flightless magical bird  native to the island of mauritius in the  indian ocean while muggles believed this  bird to be extinct in reality it existed  and had the ability to disappear and  reappear elsewhere as a means of  escaping danger similar to apparition 7.  a rumpant the rumpant is a large grey  african beast of great power weighing up  to a ton the erumpent may be mistaken  for a rhinoceros at a distance it has a  thick hind that repels most charms and  curses a large sharp horn upon its nose  and a long rope-like tail  8. fupa the fupa was a magical african  bird with brightly coloured feathers  which could include orange pink lime  green and yellow  listening to the frupa's high-pitched  twittering song would drive the listener  insane  9. giant dung beetles the giant dung  beetle was a large magical insect it is  mostly unknown how it was different from  its non-magical cousin however it was  significantly larger and could use the  three large horns on its head to carry  balls of dung instead of rolling them an  action which it could still perform  10. glow bugs glow bugs were small  luminescent magical worms 11. grap horns  the grap horn is found in mountainous  european regions large and grayish  purple with a humped back the grap horn  has two very long sharp horns walks on  large four-thumbed feet and has an  extremely aggressive nature  12. grindelow's a grindelobe is a small  horned pale green-skinned water demon  native to great britain and ireland  13. lucrota the lucrota resembled a  large moose with very long jagged  antlers and an impossibly huge mouth in  respect to its head and face it was  capable of stretching its jaws wide  enough that a full-grown human could fit  inside 14. marmite the name of this one  is hilarious the marmite was a  mode